# A service, not a topic -- deliberate, narrow exception to this project's
# "messages, not services" convention (see doc/ai/01_architecture.md's
# Notes section and doc/ai/05_migration_guide.md's "Cross-Node Access to
# Complex/Large Internal State"). planner_node hosts this; save_node calls
# it only when it has independently decided to render+save the wmodel debug
# images (its own equivalent of legacy save_thread's write_wmodel/
# SAVE_PERIOD_WMGRIF gating) -- restoring legacy's pull-based
# threads.checkData() semantics instead of planner_node pushing on its own
# schedule. planner_node never calls WMGrid::drawGrid()/drawGridFull()
# itself -- legacy keeps those exclusive to save_thread, out of
# process_thread's real-time loop, and that split stays 1:1 here too.

# Request: empty -- "give me the current wmodel state", nothing to parameterize.
---
# Response: raw WMGrid/WorldModel state (wmodel.h, istrorsx_core) at the
# moment of the call. save_node reconstructs its own WorldModel instance
# from this and draws locally.

# WMGrid::g, WMGRID_HEIGHT x WMGRID_WIDTH (2001x2001), one byte per cell --
# same flat cv::Mat-serialization convention as CameraFrame.msg (width /
# height / cv_type / step / data).
int32   grid_width
int32   grid_height
int32   grid_cv_type
int32   grid_step
uint8[] grid_data

float32 grid_x0   # WMGrid's own grid-origin tracking (recenter())
float32 grid_y0

int64   image_number     # WorldModel::image_number -- the processing tick that last updated this grid
float32 last_x0          # WorldModel::last_x0/y0/alfa -- robot pose at that last update
float32 last_y0
float32 last_alfa
int32   last_ref
int32   last_angle
int32   last_angle_min
int32   last_angle_max
